            "review_text": "EatDrinknbMarried\nMelbourne, Australia470 contributions\n0\nGood udon\nMay 2018 • Couples\nWe had the number 3 udon which was ground pork and some spice in the broth. It was good, and the size small was enough vs. the large. The udon noodles were slightly over cooked but good, and nice broth. We had tempura and wouldn’t recommend. The only tempura that was ok was eel and shrimp and that was average. the pork was tough and the sausage seemed raw. The stools aren’t very comfortable for too long, either. 3 overall thanks to the decent udon and broth\nRead more\nWritten May 23, 2018",
